{"author":{"id":"585844baa6074d44d241f46aa7c9f21ff46653adf617d7f070fbfe327626c989"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794823416,"nonce":"+3pctT6NF8gTEx1PzoncASHWoew=","message":"Decided 2026-11-16:\n- hxn-gpu is a plain haxelib with no Rust crate and no binding. Its haxelib.json depends on hxn and hxnsl only. A program adds -lib for each driver it wants (hxn-gpu-metal, -vulkan, -d3d12, -gles, -webgpu, -webgl2). hxn.Bind fails at compile time on a driver with no library for the platform, so listing all six as dependencies would break every build. hxn-gpu compiles a backend only for the drivers present, checks each driver's version at compile time, and at run time takes the first backend that opens (WebGPU before WebGL2).\n- First release: all six backends, offscreen. Buffers, textures, samplers, bind groups from hxnsl's LAYOUT, compute and render pipelines, command encoders, async readback, and one barrier tracker for Vulkan and D3D12. Compute is reported unavailable on GLES and WebGL2. Presenting to a window or canvas comes after.\n- Driver gaps to fill: hxn-gpu-vulkan has no texture upload (no copyBufferToImage) and no swapchain.\n- Repository: hx-n/hxn-gpu, created once the first version passes.","files":null}]}